# Line-ending policy for the production build inputs.
#
# The production builders generate a candidate whose bytes must be a pure
# function of the source commit. They canonicalize line endings themselves and
# fail closed if a stray carriage return survives, so this file is a second
# layer rather than the only defence: it keeps the stored blobs and every
# checkout consistent, so a working copy on any platform feeds the builders
# the same bytes git recorded.
#
# Scoped deliberately to build inputs and the builders themselves. Files
# outside this list (validate.ps1 in particular, where CRLF is the native
# convention) keep whatever they already use.

apps/*.groovy                    text eol=lf
packageManifest.json             text eol=lf
production-release-notes.txt     text eol=lf
tools/production-builder/*.groovy text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never line-ending converted, never diffed as text.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.mp3    binary
*.woff2  binary

# Vendored libraries are served to browsers with an SRI integrity hash pinned
# in the app source. Any line-ending conversion changes the bytes, the hash
# stops matching, and every browser silently refuses the file. Treated as
# binary so git never rewrites them in either direction.
public/vendor/** -text
